From bb2f08ef0884718da357a1a3b761cefc23f18099 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleg Komarov <oleg@blender.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Jan 2026 12:35:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] BLENDER: contributor agreement support

New models ContributorAgreement and SignedContributorAgreement are
introduced.

A new Settings > Contributor Agreements page is introduced.
The page allows a user to review the text of existing contributor
agreements and to sign any of them.

A new /api/v1/users/{username}/contributor-agreements/{slug} endpoint
allows to check if a user has signed a contributor agreement.
This api endpoint can be used by a gitea action workflow as described in
https://projects.blender.org/infrastructure/clacheck-runner

SignContributorAgreement function searches for failed cla.yml workflows
that were triggered by the current user and reruns them (search limited to
10 latest workflow runs).
This updates the failed check status automatically and doesn't require any
additional actions from the user.

The runner code https://projects.blender.org/infrastructure/clacheck-runner
automatically posts a pull request comment when a check fails:

    @username please sign the contributor agreement $CLA_SLUG at
    https://projects.blender.org/user/settings/contributor_agreements
